1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:02,387
The Evolution of Fashion.

2
00:00:02,337 --> 00:00:07,337
Clothing originated for protection but quickly became a marker of social status.

3
00:00:07,337 --> 00:00:11,087
Ancient Rome restricted purple dye to the emperor alone.

4
00:00:11,087 --> 00:00:18,037
Fashion as rapid, seasonal change emerged in 14th-century Europe alongside expanding trade networks.

5
00:00:18,037 --> 00:00:26,362
The sewing machine, patented by Elias Howe in 1846, democratized fashionable clothing by reducing production costs.

6
00:00:26,362 --> 00:00:32,962
The 20th century transformed fashion into a global industry driven by seasonal collections and mass media.

7
00:00:32,962 --> 00:00:37,150
Today, fast fashion brands release new styles weekly.

8
00:00:37,150 --> 00:00:46,325
The average garment is worn only seven times before disposal, and textile production accounts for approximately 10 percent of global carbon emissions.

9
00:00:46,325 --> 00:00:52,450
Consumer awareness is gradually shifting demand toward sustainable, ethically produced alternatives.

